### Client Components

There are two ways to fetch data in Client Components, using:

1. A community library like [SWR](https://swr.vercel.app/) or [React Query](https://tanstack.com/query/latest)
2. React's [`use` API](https://react.dev/reference/react/use)

#### Streaming data with the `use` API

You can use React's [`use` API](https://react.dev/reference/react/use) to [stream](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/data-fetching/fetching-caching-and-revalidating#streaming) data from the server to client. Start by fetching data in your Server component, and pass the promise to your Client Component as prop:

```tsx
import Posts from '@/app/ui/posts'
import { Suspense } from 'react'

export default function Page() {
  // Don't await the data fetching function
  const posts = getPosts()

  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading...</div>}>
      <Posts posts={posts} />
    </Suspense>
  )
}

```

```jsx
